From de6e2c2fe9e02a9f70a5ff6f313aa45abc43b84c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 04:25:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 98/98] guard telemetry: park the reader with no device work
 while the engine is idle

The bounds-guard reader (default warn) copied its counters every 0.05 s
forever, and that device-to-host copy alone holds an idle card in P2
(community issue #2). The worker now wraps execute_model, sample_tokens
and execute_dummy_batch in guard_telemetry.engine_call (call generation
plus open-call count under one lock; no device work on the engine
thread). With no call open for a full interval the reader records a
fence event on the engine stream, keeps polling until it completes,
reads every counter once more (no producer is running, so the read is
coherent), reports, and parks on a condition variable until the next
engine call. Hits from the last step before idle are reported and fatal
sites armed before it parks.

- Single-stream invariant enforced at run time: every engine call and
  every eager guarded launch must run on the engine thread and a fenced
  stream; any violation falls back to always-poll with an ERROR line.
- Count-based fatal decisions arm on the first copy that shows them; the
  WARNING with the maxima follows on the confirming copy. Detection is
  cadence-bound (armed about 1-2 intervals after the hit, reported about
  2-3, raised at the next execute_model).
- The final drain's waits are cancellable by a resumed call, a stop or a
  suspend request.
- Lifecycle: shutdown joins the reader before the final drain and a later
  worker in the same process gets a fresh reader; Worker.sleep() suspends
  the reader after synchronising the device (one settled read, no reader
  CUDA call until wake_up(); a timed-out suspend makes sleep raise).
- VLLM_E2_GUARD_IDLE (default 1) is registered and listed with the guard
  knobs as an ignored compile factor; 0, or a worker without the wiring,
  keeps the always-poll reader.

Same engine change as the guard fix in the Qwen3.8-27B series (0012
revision 2).
